holder","Gaston de Desirae"],["expansion","The House de Desirae has won several times; its present success is owed to Prince Dakkar, the son of our king. It was Prince Dakkar who restored the prestige of necromancy among the Elves, which led the Conclave to lift the last bans on practising it. After that Ball, however, unpleasant events followed: the House de Doucer, or rather its Head, Armando, acted with extraordinary baseness and brought about the death of the prince's bride, a flagrant violation of the rules of the Great Game. Louis de Desirae seized on this to declare the House de Doucer outlaw and confiscated its home allod, Nocturn.\nSo the House de Desirae now owns two allods: little Tenebra and vast Nocturn."]],"l":{"place":[["quests/r171869","Положение при дворе: Маркиз"]]},"p":[["ae39403e40d93327",1024,557]],"m":{"credit":"Allods atlas and community lore material compiled by Makar Terentiev (DarkyAndSparky), https://github.com/DarkyAndSparky/atlas-ao","translated":"Community text, translated by Allodex","source":"atlas-ao server/seed-data.json, ATLAS ALLODS.docx","name_official":true}},"a-a072":{"t":[],"s":"Mentioned island","f":[["faction","League allod"],["category","Mentioned island"],["holder","Great Martyr Ferr (Great Mage)"]],"m":{"credit":"Allods atlas and community lore material compiled by Makar Terentiev (DarkyAndSparky), https://github.com/DarkyAndSparky/atlas-ao","translated":"Community text, translated by Allodex","source":"atlas-ao server/seed-data.json","name_official":false}},"a-a077":{"t":[],"s":"Mentioned island","f":[["faction","Imperial allod"],["category","Mentioned island"],["holder","Great Martyr Hos (Great Mage)"]],"m":{"credit":"Allods atlas and community lore material compiled by Makar Terentiev (DarkyAndSparky), https://github.com/DarkyAndSparky/atlas-ao","translated":"Community text, translated by Allodex","source":"atlas-ao server/seed-data.json","name_official":false}},"a-a079":{"t":[["atlasDescription",0,0,{"md":true}]],"s":